setup`, and `verify-identity`. `reconcile` plus `reconcile-check` are excluded because their dependency-ordered migration is separate.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Remove `bridge-status` from `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py:534-543`, `bridge-fsck` from `:544-551`, and `bridge-probe` from its `bridge-probe` registry entry beginning at `:610` (anchor by command name if line numbers drift). Remove `verify-authorship` factory/handler entries at `:432/:460` and `jira-onboard` factory/handler entries at `:438/:466` (anchor by command name if line numbers drift). Do not touch `_reconcile`.\n2. Retire alias-only parser, factory, and help wiring. Each old spelling must produce argparse's standard invalid-choice error at parse time with exit code 2. It must not invoke a handler. Each canonical spelling keeps its current owner plus exit behavior.\n3. Regenerate outputs with `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`, `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`, `scripts/build_cloud_adf_corpus.py`, and `scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py`.\n4. Run the exact five-spelling string scan in the final acceptance criterion. Classify each match. Replace alias-success tests with invalid-choice tests. Retarget behavior-preserving invocations to canonical commands. Remove retired names from route census collections. Regenerate fixture matches.\n5. Replace removed commands in maintained operational prose. Preserve historical ADR plus release-note references as history.\n\n## File Impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py`, advanced bridge/Jira/verify parser factories, alias help routing — registrations plus alias-only parser wiring; delete the now-orphaned bridge-fsck/bridge-probe parser arms while retaining the shared Jira setup parser for canonical `bridge setup`\n- `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`, `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`, `scripts/build_cloud_adf_corpus.py`, `scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py` plus generated help/reference/ADF/wiki outputs\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_authorship.py` — source-emitted operational remediation text must say `verify-identity` instead of the removed `verify-authorship` command\n- `docs/cli-reference.md`, maintained CLI/identity/operational docs, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/release-notes.md` — current versus historical command language\n- `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_01.json`, `bodies_02.json`, `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py` — regenerated fixture plus reference contracts\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py`, `test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py`, `test_help_overview_coverage.py`, `test_schema_coverage.py` — generated/documentation contracts\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_heldout.py`, `test_bridge_vocabulary.py`, `test_bridge_vocabulary_e2e_heldout.py`, `test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py`, `test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6_heldout.py` — bridge behavior\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_registry.py`, `test_cli_registry_dispatch.py` — remove retired names from route/individual-arm census assertions\n- `tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py`, `test_identity_ac7_bff8_heldout.py` — replace direct alias-success tests with parse-rejection tests\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py`, `test_identity_ts3_117b_heldout.py`, `test_identity_3183.py`, `test_identity_3183_heldout.py`, `test_reclaim_collapse.py`, `test_enrich_drain.py` — retarget live `verify-authorship` subprocess calls to `verify-identity`\n- `tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py` — migrate any current command fixture to the canonical spelling\n- `tests/unit/test_bug_review_tier.py` — classify or retarget the synthetic `bridge-status` fixture match surfaced by the five-spelling scan so it is not an unclassified current-command reference\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The registry contains no `bridge-status` entry.\n- [ ] The registry contains no `bridge-fsck` entry.\n- [ ] The registry contains no `bridge-probe` entry.\n- [ ] The registry contains no `jira-onboard` entry.\n- [ ] The registry contains no `verify-authorship` entry.\n- [ ] `bridge-status` is treated as the sole hidden alias in migration history.\n- [ ] The other four spellings are treated as visible aliases in migration history.\n- [ ] Each removed spelling produces argparse invalid-choice exit code 2.\n- [ ] No removed spelling reaches its handler.\n- [ ] `bridge status` preserves current owner plus exit behavior.\n- [ ] `bridge fsck` preserves current owner plus exit behavior.\n- [ ] `bridge check-access` preserves current owner plus exit behavior.\n- [ ] `bridge setup` preserves current owner plus exit behavior.\n- [ ] `verify-identity` preserves current owner plus exit behavior.\n- [ ] Regenerated CLI help omits each removed command.\n- [ ] Regenerated CLI reference omits each removed command.\n- [ ] Regenerated Cloud ADF corpus omits each removed command.\n- [ ] Regenerated Data Center wiki corpus omits each removed command.\n- [ ] Each listed route-census test removes retired names.\n- [ ] Each listed alias-success test becomes an invalid-choice test.\n- [ ] Each listed subprocess invocation uses a canonical command.\n- [ ] `rg -l -e \"bridge-status\" -e \"bridge-fsck\" -e \"bridge-probe\" -e \"jira-onboard\" -e \"verify-authorship\" tests` is run after the migration.\n- [ ] Every remaining scan match is one of: an explicit invalid-choice test; a regenerated fixture; or historical migration evidence.\n- [ ] Maintained operational prose uses canonical commands.\n- [ ] Historical ADR plus release references retain old spellings only as historical evidence.\n- [ ] Changelog/release material records each pre-1.0 replacement.\n- [ ] `reconcile` plus `reconcile-check` remain outside this ticket.\n- [ ] Focused CLI tests pass.\n- [ ] Focused interface tests pass.\n- [ ] Documentation-generation checks pass.\n- [ ] Lint passes.\n- [ ] Typecheck passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py","reason":"remove hidden alias regi